WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.840
Godzilla Vs. Kong is finally out in&nbsp;
the world, and while most people are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.240
paying attention to the eponymous Titans, the&nbsp;
film has more than just these two Monsters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.000
Here are five characters from the film who&nbsp;
are more important than you probably realize.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.040
In the last few years, podcasts and podcasters&nbsp;
have increasingly grown in popularity, and as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.000
volume of podcasts increases, so, too, does the&nbsp;
number of podcasters becoming household names.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.680
It seems safe to say that by the end&nbsp;
of Godzilla vs. Kong, Bernie Hayes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.720
played by Brian Tyree Henry, is about to become&nbsp;
the most famous podcaster in the world of kaiju.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.920
By the time we're introduced to Bernie,&nbsp;
he's already dedicated several hundred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.880
episodes worth of podcast time to exploring the&nbsp;
conspiracies behind Monarch and giant monsters.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.920
If Bernie's podcast was popular before the events&nbsp;
of Godzilla vs Kong, then imagine how popular he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.400
will be after playing an active role in helping&nbsp;
the two monsters defeat Mechagodzilla — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.560
imagine how informed the public at large&nbsp;
will be about Monarch and their shenanigans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.800
And while we're on the subject&nbsp;
of Monarch's giant robots...

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.160
There aren't exactly villains in Godzilla vs. Kong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.200
so much as there are antagonists who&nbsp;
think they're doing something smart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.240
only to wind up hoisted by their own&nbsp;
egomania. Ren Serizawa , played by Shun Oguri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.120
is one-half of a duo of bad guys whose belief&nbsp;
is very simple: in order for humanity to thrive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.680
they must prove themselves to be a stronger,&nbsp;
collective apex predator than any giant monster.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.560
The creation of Mechagodzilla using the combined&nbsp;
might of King Ghidorah's brain and the human mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.640
may have failed, but that doesn't mean it will&nbsp;
be the last effort made toward a similar end. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.600
while Ren seems pretty dead by the end of Godzilla&nbsp;
vs. Kong, that doesn't mean his story is over.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.080
We could always see a prequel story explaining&nbsp;
how Ren came to create Mechagodzilla. Ren is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.120
after all, the son of Ken&nbsp;
Watanabe's Ishirō Serizawa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.680
who was much more of the opinion&nbsp;
that humanity should play its part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.040
in the world by sometimes standing back&nbsp;
and letting the giant monsters fight.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.800
"Let them fight."

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.829
What caused Ren to employ a&nbsp;
decidedly opposing tactic?

00:01:53.829 --> 00:01:56.320
Not to restate things, but Godzilla vs. Kong is

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.560
primarily focused on the stories of two&nbsp;
giant monsters. However, Nathan Lind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.040
played by Alexander Skarsgård, has a backstory&nbsp;
way too important not to flesh out later.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.640
When Lind is approached by Walter Simmons&nbsp;
about his potential involvement in traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.800
to the center of Hollow Earth, we get a&nbsp;
very brief mention of his past attempt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.640
What we know is that Lind's brother died in&nbsp;
an attempt to get the kaiju stomping grounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.360
but we don't really know how that happened. We&nbsp;
don't know why Lind is fixated on Hollow Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.640
we don't know how he became affiliated&nbsp;
with Monarch, and we didn't see him fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.800
out with the organization either. That&nbsp;
story is at least worth a tie-in comic.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.440
But much like Ren, the other reason why Lind is so&nbsp;
important is that it's his ideas that helped drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.520
the journey to Hollow Earth in the first place.&nbsp;
It seems likely that Lind will play an important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.000
role in understanding, and even benefiting&nbsp;
from, Hollow Earth in forthcoming stories.

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:46.080
Ilene Andrews, played by Rebecca Hall is&nbsp;
the reason King Kong stays safe for as long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.640
as he does — she is his guardian in many&nbsp;
ways. The containment area Kong calls home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.840
exists in part because of Andrews,&nbsp;
and the safeguards used to keep Kong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.360
safe as he travels to Hollow Earth&nbsp;
are a result of her care as well.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.040
When we see Hollow Earth, one of the things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.320
we notice straight away is that there&nbsp;
is even more monster life down there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.320
And if there's anyone who can catalog and&nbsp;
understand that life, it's Ilene Andrews.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.000
Andrews is important for the future of this&nbsp;
franchise precisely because she'll likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.560
stand opposed to the "destroy all monsters"&nbsp;
edict of the antagonists. And if she takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.560
on more power at Monarch in the wake of this&nbsp;
story, any attempts to build mechs will likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.280
be tempered by Andrews' level head and respect&nbsp;
for all of nature's creatures, including Kong.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.480
All that being said, there is&nbsp;
one character in Godzilla vs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.920
Kong who stands head and shoulders&nbsp;
above the entire rest of the cast:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.160
Jia, played by Kaylee Hottle. To say that&nbsp;
Jia's empathy and ability to communicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.040
with Kong literally saved all of humanity's&nbsp;
collective bacon is probably an understatement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.520
And she's only going to become more important for&nbsp;
humans and monsters alike both as she gets older.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:48.000
If you recall, in Kong: Skull Island, the island&nbsp;
is home to more than just the big ape — there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.920
also a tribe of people living symbiotically&nbsp;
with him. And while Kong protects those people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.080
they also respect and watch out for him.&nbsp;
We find out in Godzilla vs. Kong that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.680
only surviving member of that tribe is&nbsp;
Jia and it's through her ability to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.480
sign language that humanity learns Kong isn't&nbsp;
just intelligent but also able to communicate.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.640
Jia is so in tune with Kong that she can feel&nbsp;
his heart slow down to the point of death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.560
Without her, he wouldn't even be alive right&nbsp;
now. It's hard to say that there's anyone else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.320
who could convince Kong to fight for the&nbsp;
human race at this point other than Jia.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.560
Similarly, we may discover that other monsters&nbsp;
are able to communicate through sign language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.760
As she gets older, it seems likely&nbsp;
that Jia may not only be the person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.160
best able to understand these creatures;&nbsp;
she may also be their strongest advocate.

